      "fp.scan-barcode.kicker": "Barcode scan",
      "fp.scan-barcode.h1": "Packaged food, <em class=\"accent\">already solved</em>.",
      "fp.scan-barcode.lead": "Point the camera at the barcode on any packet and the nutrition comes straight back — calories, macros, the ingredient list and the allergens, read from a large product database rather than estimated. It is free, it is unlimited, and it never touches your AI scan allowance.",
      "fp.scan-barcode.shotAlt": "A phone scanning the barcode on a packet, with the product's nutrition appearing beside it",
      "fp.scan-barcode.stepsKicker": "How it works",
      "fp.scan-barcode.stepsTitle": "Four seconds, <em class=\"accent\">most of them holding the packet</em>.",
      "fp.scan-barcode.stepsSub": "Anything with a barcode is the easy case. There is no estimating involved — the numbers come off the product record.",
      "fp.scan-barcode.getKicker": "What you get",
      "fp.scan-barcode.getTitle": "Label numbers, without reading the label.",
      "fp.scan-barcode.getSub": "Everything on the back of the pack, in a form you can actually compare and track.",
      "fp.scan-barcode.recKicker": "Where it earns its keep",
      "fp.scan-barcode.recTitle": "Two products, one decision, four seconds.",
      "fp.scan-barcode.recBody": "The real use for barcode scanning is not logging — it is deciding. Standing in an aisle with a packet in each hand is the moment a nutrition label is worth something, and it is also the moment nobody reads one.",
      "fp.scan-barcode.faqTitle": "Questions about barcode scanning",
      "fp.scan-barcode.ctaTitle": "Scan the packet. Skip the small print.",
      "fp.scan-barcode.ctaBody": "Fotocal is free to start, with a 5-day free trial on the paid plans.",
      "fp.scan-barcode.relatedTitle": "Keep reading",
      "fp.scan-barcode.relatedSub": "How to get more out of what is printed on the pack.",
      "fp.scan-barcode.navLabel": "Scan barcode",
      "fp.scan-barcode.bandAlt": "A hand holding a phone up to the barcode on a packet of granola, a similar packet on the shelf beside it",
      "fp.scan-barcode.bandPill": "In practice",
      "fp.scan-barcode.bandTitle": "Two packets, one aisle, four seconds",
      "fp.scan-barcode.bandBody": "The front of the pack is marketing. The back is small print you were never going to read standing up in a supermarket. Scan both codes, compare what they actually contain, put one back.",
      "fp.scan-barcode.s1t": "Point at the barcode",
      "fp.scan-barcode.s1b": "Anywhere on the pack, any angle you can hold it at. It reads as soon as the code is in frame.",
      "fp.scan-barcode.s2t": "The product comes back",
      "fp.scan-barcode.s2b": "Name, brand and the full nutrition record, pulled from the database rather than worked out from a photo.",
      "fp.scan-barcode.s3t": "Set the amount",
      "fp.scan-barcode.s3b": "Per 100 g, per the serving printed on the label, or the amount you are actually having. Half a packet is half a packet.",
      "fp.scan-barcode.s4t": "Log it to a meal",
      "fp.scan-barcode.s4b": "Straight into Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner or Snack, where it joins everything else in the day.",
      "fp.scan-barcode.c1t": "Instant identification",
      "fp.scan-barcode.c1b": "The product recognised by its barcode, so there is no searching, no near-miss database entries and no picking between eight versions of the same yoghurt.",
      "fp.scan-barcode.c2t": "Calories",
      "fp.scan-barcode.c2b": "The headline number, for the amount you set rather than only per 100 g.",
      "fp.scan-barcode.c3t": "Full macro breakdown",
      "fp.scan-barcode.c3b": "Protein, carbs and fat, straight into the day's rings.",
      "fp.scan-barcode.c4t": "The ingredient list",
      "fp.scan-barcode.c4b": "What is actually in it, in the order it is in it — which is often more revealing than the calorie count.",
      "fp.scan-barcode.c5t": "Allergens",
      "fp.scan-barcode.c5b": "Called out from the product record, so you are not scanning small print in a supermarket aisle.",
      "fp.scan-barcode.c6t": "Free and unlimited",
      "fp.scan-barcode.c6b": "Barcode scanning is not metered and does not consume an AI scan. Scan a whole shopping basket if you want to — it costs nothing.",
      "fp.scan-barcode.r1": "Scan both and compare the actual numbers instead of the marketing on the front of the pack.",
      "fp.scan-barcode.r2": "Because it is unlimited and free, there is no reason not to scan something you are only considering.",
      "fp.scan-barcode.r3": "Anything you do log feeds the same day totals, rings and Weekly Report as a photographed meal.",
      "fp.scan-barcode.r4": "Coach Kal can see your logged packaged foods, so “why is my sodium high this week?” has a real answer rather than a guess.",
      "fp.scan-barcode.q1": "Is barcode scanning included in the free plan?",
      "fp.scan-barcode.a1": "Yes, and it is unlimited. It is not a trial feature, it is not capped per day, and it does not use up AI scans.",
      "fp.scan-barcode.q2": "Does it use my AI scan quota?",
      "fp.scan-barcode.a2": "No. Barcode lookups and AI photo scans are completely separate. Scanning a hundred barcodes leaves your AI scans untouched.",
      "fp.scan-barcode.q3": "What if a product is not in the database?",
      "fp.scan-barcode.a3": "It happens, particularly with small local brands. You can photograph the food instead, or add the item by hand from the label — either way you are not stuck.",
      "fp.scan-barcode.q4": "Does it work outside my country?",
      "fp.scan-barcode.a4": "The database is international and covers a very large range of packaged products, so most supermarket items scan wherever you are. Regional and own-brand products are the most likely gaps.",
